g on 14 October because investor demand fell short (n6.d10 and the Pellham statement). Its 2027 capital spending is planned up 18%. In response it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40%, resize its Q1 2027 tender (about C$900M) and defer two substation programmes \"until financing improves\". The capex plan is therefore being cut to fit the financing, not the other way round.\n- **Norvane:** Its 2027 spending is planned up 12%, with a C$450M tender in Q2. The tracker says two utility share offerings were cut back in Q3, but I found no detail on the second one. I found no Norvane equity target, so I can't say how big its equity gap is.\n- **Issuance appetite:** Weak. Investor demand was insufficient even for a C$2.4B deal, and two offerings were cut back in Q3.\n- **Wider funding conditions:** Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp (n5.d5, n5.d7). Debt is getting more expensive as well, so debt is not a clean substitute.\n\n**Implication for VLTX:** VLTX won 60% of the last tender round, and Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria. A roughly 40% cut in Pellham's transformer orders is therefore a direct risk to 2027 order intake. I did not check how much of VLTX's orders Pellham accounts for.\n\n**Gaps:** I found no data on utility valuations, equity needs by company, or any re-launch timing for the Pellham deal. I would treat a re-launch as a possibility, not an expectation.","ttft_ms":1416,"type":"result","duration_ms":33404,"uuid":"1eaacdaf-20ce-448e-b04e-14cdd546c602","ttft_stream_ms":932,"time_to_request_ms":53,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":6,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":1,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":5,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":2,"message_